In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
And leaves my tongue doth give.
Yet, in our errors, I find a kind of praise,
A kind of praise, as mine in love's sweet name.
But what of thee that I hope to find a kind of praise,
Where words of thee, the truth would give life anew.
And what of thee that I bring forth,
Thy name with beauty would be my own defeat,
And by their verdict, I am proved.
  For thee, dear friend, I sing of thee,
  As I would attest, the love of thy worth.


