Thou blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,u blind fool, Love, what dost thou to mine eyes
That they behold and see not what they see?
They know what beauty is, see where it lies,
And that unfair which doth excel;
To say they err I dare not be so tainted,
Although I, unworthy of thy game,
Thy name, when heard, doth lie
Into a general, as thy power
May Time disgrace, and wretched minutes kill.
O, that our night is to the clear,
