Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch to the view,
She plays the game of feigned innocence.
But I, the humble clouds, the rain,
Of marrows 'twixt a miserly act,
My heart, with love, does sail with pride.
My eyes, once bright, have lost their way,
In the tumult of this endless night.
Oh, cruel revelation of my heart's deceit,
That taught me how to ruminate,
A solace stronger than before.
  So I return, and then return it love,
  That every trial leaves me stronger, if I dare.


