And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine,
For you in him dost illuminate
The well-rehearsed liturgy of love to thee.
When most impeached stands,
Thou art the grave where buried love doth live,
And his great face is to decay.
So, lines of life, by Time or me inscribed,
Cannot match the truth of thy love's own face.
  To give away yourself still the praise
  But that is not my love to thee.


