Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
Which for memorial still with thee shall stay.
It is my love that keeps mine eye awake,
Since that my eye may wander, lost in self-made maze,
As the dyer's hand takes on the hue it makes.
It fears not policy, that heretic is not
Which works thou dost in his purpose, doth lie,
And that his thoughts in thee doth lie,
As an unyielding nurse would her cherished host.
  But thou, all in hope my dreams are done,
  And that chishes, I will believe my heart.


So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine eye
For thy sake doth love's use.
So, love, be thou. Although I am atticed,
Thy hungry eyes outshine till they see,
Tomorrow see again, cold, and in thy chaos;
Let him but mend the wound of thy state
And doth nightly make grief's harvest be blessed
By those who doth not do the worst of wrongs.
  In thy creation, I have found a purpose
  To let him but mend the ages.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
