When my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,n my love swears that she is made of truth
I do believe her though I know she lies,
That she might think me some untutored youth,
To admit your face is well-killed.
But why should I reproach you for two breaches,
When I am guilty of the world's turned?
My vows, but tools to bring you to my reaches,
My faith, a shadow, fleeting and cold.
For I have sworn by your profound kindness,
By your affection, loyalty, and trust;
Yet blinded by desire, I twist and bend,
Truth's enemy, in deceit I am immersed.
  For I have painted you as fair, blinded eye,
  To lie against the truth, so vile and unworthy.


O, call not me to justify the wrong
That thy unkindness lays upon my heart;
Wound me not with thine eye but with thy tongue;call not me to justify the wrong
That thy unkindness lays upon my heart;
Wound me not with thine eye but with thy tongue;
Thy adverse party is my sense.
O, to thyself I are no other bards conspire,
Whose greatest is thy good report,
And in thy chaos doth see thee frown,
Who hath taught it to reshape and seep,
That I hath writ thee for my sake,
Be absent, and hath no rest.
What force can mine own love to me
That I should spurn thee than is due?
  But yet, love, you alone might
  As high as any heart, by thee.


Be wise as thou art cruel; do not press
My tongue-tied patience with too much disdain,
Lest sorrow lend me words, and words expresswise as thou art cruel; do not press
My tongue-tied patience with too much disdain,
Lest sorrow lend me words, and words express,
Thy merit hath taught it to reshape and seep,
Into the vile, a heavenly grace to cast,
A beauty like your own, from dross to rise,
In every dark, a brilliance to outlast,
As shadows flee before the dawn's embrace.
Alas, what refuge for the gems thou dost withhold,
Shall keep me from the darkness, deep inside,
As on your welcoming surface, I am only winning.
  For thee, against myself I sing,
  For thee, dear friend, time's illusions sift.


In faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,faith, I do not love thee with mine eyes,
For they in thee a thousand errors note;
But 'tis my heart that loves what they despise,
Defying the judgment of displeased sight it draws.
Neither are my ears enchanted by your voice's song,
Nor are gentle emotions inclined to the lowly touch;
Nor does taste or scent, crave to be part of where they belong,
In any sensual banquet with you as the crutch.
Yet my five senses and my five faculties cannot,
Dissuade one foolish heart from being enslaved by thee,
Remaining steadfast, the semblance of a man is caught,
Thy haughty heart's thrall, a wretched servant to be.
  Only my affliction, thus far


Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
Unless it turned to iron or was something more.
For if it err, not from those lips that preach,
Stained scarred, mine eye no longer held,
Gilding the dyer's hand at his feet.
Let those who bear no pain,
Harsh, featureless, and hollow, fade without,
Look to those she blessed, let them find out,
Bounteous nurse who with thee fell a care.
  In nothing's hand, the rose's will stand,
  And through them, their youthful dreams.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch to the chase,
She plays the game of feigned innocence.
But if you find such wealth, where you choose not possess,
Or brings you joy to the end.
For if you find this worth,
Years would not steal the bloom of youth away.
Let those who bear no fruit, in drought,
Harsh, featureless, and hollow, fade without,
Look to those she blessed, let them find out,
Bounteous gifts to cherish, to bear without.
  She carved you for her sign, her truth,
  To propagate, not let that copy soothe.


