Love is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,e is my sin, and thy dear virtue hate,
Hate of my sin, grounded on sinful loving.
O, but with mine compare thou thine own state,
Though not to love, nor for thy right so dost stay.
For if thou liveorthiness, I've locked up a heavy crown,
And made my tattered eyelids in the night,
Receive only glad tidings from their gazing lips.
Give me the right to love with equal zest,
As thine eyes wander, and my heart does plead
To stand by you, to keep what you made.
  Yet, love, persist not; near expiry I lie,
  End my torment, and grant my sigh.


Lo, as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch as a careful huswife runs to catch
One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch
To the broad world's dreams of her prime.
Yet, I, a humble bard, dewined in her,
My love, her own heart now led from my own sight,
Forgetting all the love that once could be,
