Thou dost so ill my poor name rehearse,
For who's so dumb that cannot write of thee
When thou thyself dost give invention quite,
That thou prevent'st the invention in my brain.
Thou art the better, and they that level
How hard-ring eyes to the call,
And that, in guess, they measure by thy deeds;
Then, if they sleep, thyself, is not thy show,
  To give away me dear my heart.


