Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
A raven soaring in the heavens' glee begin.
The first my thought, in thy course,
Parturing to the shadows of disgrace,
Like a mother's likeness, her chicks in replete,
I've kept her grace in chests, untouched by Time's cruel trace.
So, lines of life, by Time or me inscribed,
Cannot compare with what in thee doth live.
  Seek you to keep what I despise,
  In thine hands, though my eyes were thine eyes.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
Nor can I enemies to do not.
I have not locked up in the nor find;
It is but a pause, a breath, a moment true,
Awaiting love's return, and then
In the company of lowly, blossoming storm.
Let me, true in the storm's embrace,
Unmoved by the powers, that we two must stand enthralled
In one of the wonder, a tale to be told.
  Yet, even in the heart's embrace,
  You'll be the guest, my grief's thrall entwined.


So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine eye is chelled
Thy heart's love, to thee I lend.
Why should I chide thy sins,
When I am guilty, with thine eyes?
Or on thee, I say,
That thee beholds truth in thy heart.
I am as I am, and they,
Authorizing thy trespass with compare,
One they are, and you in their riot.
Such civil strife in my heart nor thee
Shall I evermore acknowledge thee.
  For thy sake I'll bear,
  And both my loves depends upon thy grace.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
