Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
And bind my dearest friend to share this grief?
It wrests me from myself, and binds
Another self, more cruelly, to your will;
Abandoned, I, that self, and you, find
Our hearts entwined in torment, thrice multiplied.
Imprison my heart within your fortress chest,
But in your breast, I start to fray,
Overwhelmed by beauty, and mine by thee.
  Yet, in your heart's vast chamber, open
  The fortress of memory, so oft as I commend.


So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
In hopes of fortune's child.
Yet, I cannot know thy fault is many a confession,
Thy adverse party is my advocate--
And in that I find a better state to grow
Than from thy walks when I have seen thee.
So is my love that keeps mine eye awake,
Mine own true love that doth my rest defeat
To play the watchman ever for thy sake.
  For thee watch I whilst thou dost wake elsewhere,
  From my own health, thou shalt come.


Whoever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,ever hath her wish, thou hast thy will,
And will to boot, and will in overplus.
More than enough am I that vex thee still,
Thy sweet love, to die well?
If I could, knowing thy will, thou art,
The well-absent praises from thee brain,
Yet this quiet find,
Thy heart'st a wretched soul,
That in thy mind, I am thy debtor, aware.
Look what thy memory cannot contain
Commit to these waste blanks, and thou shalt find
Those children nursed, delivered from thy brain,
To take a new acquaintance of thy mind.
  These offices, so oft as thou wilt look,
  Shall profit thee and much enrich thy book.


