Generating dev sonnets for chrF scoring...
Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
And there is thine in the plainst light.
Then can I believe thee, to keep fast my flow,
Although in the tender embrace of my every part,
I've found a purpose concealed,
And in thy chaos, I see a skies.
Who hath shown thee how to twist my heart,
To cherish more the more I see amiss?
Though I should push thee far, depart,
My heart still clings, with love grown' miss.
  If thy unworthiness hath wrought this love,
  More worthy I to be loved above.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
