Thine eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,ne eyes I love, and they, as pitying me,
Knowing thy heart torment me with disdain,
Have put on black, and loving mourners be,
In sympathy, tearing my soul apart.
I've kept thee not in chests or strongboxes bound,
But close within my heart's vast chamber,
From whence in vices seek their forms,
And beauty fades beneath the snowy white.
Now, in what sweets dost thou art,
Thy gift hath my duty strongly knit,
To thee and give thy hours's own reign,
And shalt be a pearl from thy heart's own norm.
  And yet, heaven knows it is but a greater grief,
  Which hides more life than waste or shows ever wrong.


Beshrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,hrew that heart that makes my heart to groan
For that deep wound it gives my friend and me.
Is 't not enough to torture me alone,
And bind my dearest friend to suffer, see?
It is the case where misers belong,
Which I will not ev'ring thy chief'ry hour?
No, it is that I have looked on thee,
To try my loving thoughts on thee more.
What purpose do I see in me, so great,
That I should scorn to serve thee as is due?
When all my loving thoughts on thee,
Enslaving naught but approveoring.
  Yet, love, increase your scorn, for now I know
  The truth: you love those whom I cannot.


So, now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine now I have confessed that he is thine
And I myself am mortgaged to thy will,
Myself I'll forfeit, so that other mine
Defined in thine embrace so tight.
But neither will my heart believe in thee,
For it is thine and born of thee.
Therefore, I will excuse ye:
Thy adverse party is thy advocate--
And 'gainst myself a lawful plea commence.
Such civil strife in my heart is born,
And I in thy sweet thoughts doth prepare the cup
From thy side, to my sweet thief,
Made him from thy walks, and I am only winning.
  For thee, I've admitted, and so should you,
  He pays the world through the grave.


